Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}-7 \\ 11\end{aligned}] & =[\begin{aligned}3 \\ -4\end{aligned}]+5T({v}_{2}) \\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}-7 \\ 11\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}3 \\ -4\end{aligned}] \\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}-10 \\ 15\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =\frac{1}{5}[\begin{aligned}-10 \\ 15\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}-2 \\ 3\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

